-- title:
--   A query of the batched data structure, in every program beginning with base58B
-- statement:
--   For every $R$ and standard limits, `base58B ++ R` meets `QueryAtASpec lim (base58B ++ R)`: for input arrays $A_L,A_R$ bounded by $U$ whose data structure `DSReadyA p t aX aY b0 AL AR` is in memory, the call queryAt$(I,J,b_0)$ returns within `tQueryAt p.L p.m t` steps the value of the query of Lemma 28 for the encodings of the bands of $I$ and of $J$ and the output position $(I,J)$, changing only the scratch areas. With the batched arrays of `preCoreB_base58B` this value is the inner product of a source row and a source column (`queryValue_bArray`).
--
--   The batched layout (`Batch/Tiling`): the source of the left side is a $K_0N\times D$ matrix $X$ (row by row), that of the right side a $D\times K_0N$ matrix $Y$ (stored transposed); the slot $(g,h)$ of the band $\beta$ holds the row block number $(\beta K_0+g)K_0+h$ of the source, so one run of Theorem 30's data structure computes $K_0^2$ independent block products.
